==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la}} {{term|attritio||a rubbing against|lang=la}}, from the verb {{term|attritus|lang=la}}, past participle of {{term|atterere||to wear|lang=la}}, from {{term|ad-||to, towards|lang=la}} + {{term|terere||to rub|lang=la}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|-}}

# wearing or grinding down by [[friction]]
# {{human resources}} A gradual, natural reduction in [[membership]] or [[personnel]], as through retirement, resignation, or [[death]]
# {{sciences}} The loss of [[participant]]s during an [[experiment]]

